    "body": "Autobot requires a default-branch policy before it can publish native APPROVE or REQUEST_CHANGES reviews. Without that opt-in, the workflow downgrades those verdicts to COMMENT.\n\nAdd `.github/autobot/review-config.yml` with `approval.enabled: true`. Permit active members of the existing repository engineering/maintainer and CI automation teams:\n\n- `NVIDIA-NeMo/lm_team`\n- `NVIDIA-NeMo/lm_maintainers`\n- `NVIDIA-NeMo/automation`\n\nThe policy takes effect after merge to `main`; the review service checks the requester's active team membership before publishing a formal verdict.\n\nTested:\n\n- `python3 -c 'from pathlib import Path; import yaml; p = yaml.safe_load(Path(\".github/autobot/review-config.yml\").read_text()); a = p[\"approval\"]; assert a[\"enabled\"] is True; t = a[\"eligible_teams\"]; assert isinstance(t, list) and t and all(isinstance(x, str) and x and \"/\" not in x for x in t) and len(t) == len(set(t)); print(\"approval config valid\")'` — passed YAML and approval-policy shape checks.\n- `git diff --check HEAD^ HEAD` — passed.\n- `gh api orgs/NVIDIA-NeMo/teams/<slug>` for every configured team — verified each team exists in the repository's organization.\n- `UV_NO_SYNC=1 uv run pre-commit run --all-files` — passed all applicable hooks.\n",
    "changed_files": 1,
